<title>USA: U.S. wheat weekly export sales highlights -- USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. wheat weekly export sales highlights -- USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA wheat export sales highlights in latest reporting week:</p>
<p>Wheat:  Net sales of 231,400 metric tons (MT) were 16 percent below the previous week and 44 percent under the 4-week average.  Major increases reported for Japan (86,600MT), Israel (44,900 MT), and South Korea (42,800 MT) were partly offset by decreases for unknown destinations (35,000 MT), Bangladesh (26,100 MT), and Turkey (20,000 MT).</p>
<p>Exports of 461,400 MT were one-tenth above the week earlier, but 9 percent under the 4-week average.  The primary destinations were Japan (105,800 MT), Yemen (73,500 MT), Pakistan (31,500 MT), and Turkey (30,500 MT).</p>
</text>
